# Cloudflare Pages always serves a real static file first (prerendered /learn/*, /compare/*,
# /app/current-affairs/*, /app/exam-notices/* pages) before ever consulting this file - these
# rules only run for paths with no matching file on disk.
#
# Use the extensionless fallback to avoid Cloudflare canonicalizing .html to a new URL.
# Onboarding has its own generated HTML entry.
# Known client-side-only screens (no prerendered HTML - correctly excluded from robots.txt) still
# need an explicit 200 here so real users/bookmarks/shares get the app, not a 404 interstitial.
/app/home                      /spa  200
/app/study                     /spa  200
/app/study/*                   /spa  200
/app/practice                  /spa  200
/app/practice/*                /spa  200
/app/mistakes                  /spa  200
/app/bookmarks                 /spa  200
/app/progress                  /spa  200
/app/digest                    /spa  200
/app/account                   /spa  200
/app/challenge                 /spa  200
/app/current-affairs-quiz      /spa  200
/app/current-affairs-quiz/*    /spa  200

# Everything else (typos, removed lesson slugs, old/invalid IDs) is a genuine 404 - serving the
# SPA shell with a real 404 status lets React Router show NotFoundPage while still telling Google
# and other crawlers the page doesn't exist, instead of a "soft 404" (200 on a page that says
# "not found"), which Search Console flags as a quality problem.
/*  /spa  404
